SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia Zourva Monastery (8 September)
LOCATION:Zourva\, Hydra\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The women's monastery of the Nativity of the Theotokos at Zourva\, on the far eastern tip of Hydra\, keeps its feast on 7-8 September with vespers on the eve and a liturgy with a representative of the Metropolitan. It is a two-hour walk from town over the ridge or a water taxi to the cove below\; the nuns offer coffee and sweets\, and September is the best month to do the path.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#zourva-feast-of-panagia-zourva-monastery-8-september
